WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.940
How do you feel about Georgetown’s decision to rename one of their buildings for Isaac Hawkins?

2
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.880
It’s the happiest thing.

3
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:12.020
That was one of the things I asked for when the president came.

4
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:16.920
Because he asked, “What would you like us to do?”

5
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:22.460
I said, “I’d like a family reunion [laughs] sponsored by Georgetown.”

6
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:33.220
And I said, “And I’d like for there to be some sort of remembrance or dedication for our ancestors.”

7
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:48.000
Being a dedication, dedicating a building, or just an area where you go for peace and solitude, or just something in their honor.

8
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.720
That’s all I wanted.

9
00:00:52.720 --> 00:01:03.220
It’s my understanding that part of what’s going to happen on the eighteenth is there’s going to be an official apology.

10
00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:08.000
It is what it is at that point.

11
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.160
That’s not what I’m looking for.

12
00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:14.280
I’d rather there’d be just acknowledgment.

13
00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:29.420
Acknowledgment that it was wrong, and that we know better now.

14
00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:30.560
When you know better you do better.
